
<p>Back in the primordial days of AI, Parry was an ELIZA-style chatbot created by psychiatrist Kenneth Colby to simulate the words of a paranoid schizophrenic. Someone had the genius idea to connect it to Eliza (a.k.a. “Doctor”). Vint Cerf published the transcript as an RFC in 1973, and I laughed my ass off reading it. A taste:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p><em>Do you know anything about bookies?</em></p>

<p>What makes you think I know anything about bookies?</p>

<p><em>A bookie didn’t pay me off once.</em></p>

<p>What does that suggest to you?</p>

<p><em>I beat up the bookie who did not pay off, and I thought he might use his friends in the underworld to get even with me.</em></p>

<p>What else would you like to discuss?</p>

<p><em>What do you know about racketeers?</em></p>
</blockquote>

